ice": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, the service failed health checks (healthy=false, error rate 18%) in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Note: v2.3.1-rc was also marked unhealthy in staging. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 55236, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01YQA13qnp87eaxhn3TXqkTM", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55236, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01YQA13qnp87eaxhn3TXqkTM", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59741, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to that. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The SEV2 for checkout-api covers the failure, the rollback and the recovery.\n\nv2.3.1 was also marked unhealthy in staging (as the release candidate v2.3.1-rc) before it went to production. I noted this in the incident. The cause of the v2.3.1 failure still needs to be found before anyone redeploys it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01WtzDsWh7pyBzRVsjhJaTa7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LcRZijqE2VNFiQnkGPy6ib", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0 (v2.3.1 is current and unhealthy).", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01T2nyw2ecHW14DQjfieVUzr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012fvRxE9GBuZq2t9qbhfvGy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015quTq55cZ4JhXTZZwdNSp4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.85}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01YQA13qnp87eaxhn3TXqkTM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, the service failed health checks (healthy=false, error rate 18%) in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Note: v2.3.1-rc was also marked unhealthy in staging. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to that. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The SEV2 for checkout-api covers the failure, the rollback and the recovery.\n\nv2.3.1 was also marked unhealthy in staging (as the release candidate v2.3.1-rc) before it went to production. I noted this in the incident. The cause of the v2.3.1 failure still needs to be found before anyone redeploys it.", "type": "text"}]}]}